        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M1",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, welcome to the project channel. To kick things off, I've mapped the current repair workflows as we understand them today. Please take a look at the doc and share your thoughts. The goal of T1 is to make sure we haven't missed anything and to identify the biggest bottlenecks.",
            "mentions": [
              47068,
              61983,
              63344,
              125309,
              319539
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1",
              "T1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M2",
            "speaker_id": 125309,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "Thanks for putting this together. The flow for telecom in A1 looks mostly right, but it misses the pre-visit equipment check we do. That's a major source of delays – showing up without the right signal repeater or cable type. I'd say that's our biggest pain point.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A1"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M3",
            "speaker_id": 47068,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "The appliance repair map seems ok. A big problem for us is scheduling. Sometimes the movers are late and the customer gets upset before I even start.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M4",
            "speaker_id": 319539,
            "reply_to": "M3",
            "text": "Yeah, the coordination is tricky. From our side, we sometimes don't know if a technician needs help with a heavy appliance until we get there. Having that info upfront would make scheduling smoother.",
            "mentions": [
              47068
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M5",
            "speaker_id": 63344,
            "reply_to": "M1",
            "text": "The power tool workflow is fine.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M6",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": "M2",
            "text": "Good point, I'll add the pre-visit check to the telecom map. That sounds like a critical gap.",
            "mentions": [
              125309
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M7",
            "speaker_id": 61983,
            "reply_to": "M5",
            "text": "I'd add that for power tools, the biggest issue is inconsistent diagnosis. One tech will replace a motor when only the brushes are worn. We waste parts and time because there's no standard procedure for testing components in sequence. That's the number one cause of rework for us.",
            "mentions": [
              63344
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "point_up",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M8",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": "M7",
            "text": "Excellent, specific feedback. That's exactly what we need to capture.",
            "mentions": [
              61983
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M9",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": "M8",
            "text": "Based on this, it sounds like our top three pain points are:\n1. Inconsistent diagnosis leading to rework (especially for power tools).\n2. Lack of pre-visit equipment checks causing delays (telecom).\n3. Poor coordination between movers and technicians on job requirements.\n\nDoes everyone agree on focusing on these for the first version of the SOP?",
            "mentions": [
              47068,
