      {
        "thread_id": "TH4",
        "thread_goal": "Lock in scheduling rules and customer communication approach.",
        "messages": [
          {
            "msg_id": "M46",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": null,
            "text": "Team, let's tackle scheduling and customer communication. Based on the pain points from T1, I've drafted proposals for Scheduling Rules (A5) and a Customer Communication Playbook (A7). These are meant to address T5 and T7. Please review and share your feedback.",
            "mentions": [
              47068,
              61983,
              63344,
              125309,
              319539
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "A7",
              "T5",
              "T7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M47",
            "speaker_id": 319539,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "In A5, the 30-minute travel buffer between jobs seems a bit tight for rush hour. We could end up being late for afternoon appointments.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M48",
            "speaker_id": 125309,
            "reply_to": "M47",
            "text": "I agree. Could we make the buffer dynamic? For example, 30 mins for jobs between 10am-2pm, but 45-60 mins for jobs at the start and end of the day. It's more complex to schedule but reflects reality.",
            "mentions": [
              319539
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "bulb",
                "count": 2
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M49",
            "speaker_id": 47068,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "For the communication playbook A7, the templates are good. It would be helpful to have a standard line for what to say when we find out a repair will cost more than the initial estimate.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M50",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": "M48",
            "text": "A dynamic buffer is a smart suggestion. Let's try that for the pilot routes. I'll update A5 to reflect a 45-minute buffer for jobs before 10am and after 3pm.",
            "mentions": [
              125309
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": [
              {
                "emoji": "+1",
                "count": 1
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M51",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": "M49",
            "text": "Good catch. That's a critical scenario. I'll add a section to A7 on 'Handling Quote Revisions' with a clear script for technicians to follow. Thanks for flagging that.",
            "mentions": [
              47068
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M52",
            "speaker_id": 63344,
            "reply_to": "M46",
            "text": "Who is supposed to send the 'on my way' text?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M53",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": "M52",
            "text": "The playbook A7 specifies that the technician sends it when they are leaving their previous job. It's in the 'Pre-Visit Communication' section.",
            "mentions": [
              63344
            ],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M54",
            "speaker_id": 547643,
            "reply_to": "M53",
            "text": "With those changes incorporated, are we ready to approve the scheduling rules in A5 and the communication playbook in A7 for the pilot?",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [
              "A5",
              "A7"
            ],
            "decision_refs": [
              "D7",
              "D8"
            ],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M55",
            "speaker_id": 125309,
            "reply_to": "M54",
            "text": "Yes, approved.",
            "mentions": [],
            "artifact_refs": [],
            "decision_refs": [],
            "reactions": []
          },
          {
            "msg_id": "M56",
            "speaker_id": 319539,
            "reply_to": "M54",
